# Normalise line endings in the repository, not on each contributor's machine.
#
# Without this, Git's autocrlf converts LF to CRLF on checkout for every text
# file, which makes `git diff` noisy across platforms, and — more importantly
# here — would change the bytes of any committed JSONL ledger fixture and
# therefore every digest computed over it. Digests are supposed to be
# reproducible on any machine; line-ending normalisation is part of what makes
# that true.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary

# Ledger fixtures are evidence. Hash them byte-for-byte, never normalise them.
*.jsonl -text
